<content>
  <section><title> Writing Functions from Graphs</title>
<media><image alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS 0 COMMA 4, 1 COMMA 12, AND 2 COMMA 36." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f5b8e4ad98579e421c915d6944c68bd1c9524248"/></media><para>Find the equation of the function graphed above. Then find the value at \(f(5)\).</para>
<table>
  <tgroup cols="2"><thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
          <item> Find the value of \(a\), the starting point. </item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        \(a=4\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
          <item> Find the \(b\), the growth factor. </item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        \(b=3\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
          <item> Write the equation of the function. </item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        \(f(x)=4 \cdot 3^x\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
          <item> Find \(f(5)\). </item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        \(f(5)=4 \cdot 3^5=972\)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</tgroup></table>
<title> Try It: Writing Functions from Graphs</title>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Use the graph below to write the equation of the function. Then find \(f(5)\).</para>
    <media><image alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS 0 COMMA 2, 1 COMMA 8, AND 2 COMMA 32." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/c6886dff32bbb16d44b05f5c51a3a9d21993da87"/>
    </media><para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  <para>Here is how to write the exponential function from the graph:</para>
  <table>
    <tgroup cols="2"><thead/>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>
          <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
            <item> Find the value of \(a\), the starting point. </item>
          </list>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(a=2\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
            <item> Find the \(b\), the growth factor. </item>
          </list>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(b=4\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
            <item> Write the equation of the function. </item>
          </list>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(f(x)=2 \cdot 4^x\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
            <item> Find \(f(5)\). </item>
          </list>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(f(x)=2 \cdot 4^5=2048\)
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </tgroup></table>

</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
